# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Bytecode from the signal renderers' tests under .github/scripts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Secrets — .env.example is committed, real credentials never are
.env

# Rebuildable per-project cache inside *.scor/ project directories
cache/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Snapshot comparison leaves these beside the references when a panel changed.
# The reference is committed; what a failing run produced is not, and neither
# is the reference a blessing run replaced — `.old.png` is the picture that was
# just superseded, which is a thing to look at once and never a thing to keep.
*.new.png
*.diff.png
*.old.png

# Claude Code's per-clone state. `skills/` is committed — the working protocols
# travel with the repo or they are not protocols — and nothing else here is:
# `worktrees/` is scratch checkouts measured in gigabytes, and
# `settings.local.json` is one machine's permissions.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
